From 596dc76f9c691a1a1755a2fc377f3d6df2586eec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:21:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] dshot: output-path watchdog - stop the thrusters if the
 control loop stalls

Task_DShot_RMT re-sends its cached out[]/nrm[]/armed every cycle, so a
stalled or livelocked Task_ControlLoop kept the Pico fed with fresh,
CRC-valid ARMED frames: its 150 ms link failsafe never tripped and the last
demand was held indefinitely. ControlState::loop_stamp_ms was written every
cycle and read nowhere.

The control loop now bumps ThrusterState::out_seq inside the same lock as
throttle[]/norm[]/armed. The DShot task counts consecutive cycles in which
it has not moved; at CTRL_OUT_STALE_CYCLES (10 = 20 ms) it sends the
disarmed stop (DSHOT_DISARMED / zero norm / armed=false - what the disarmed
path already sends) and queues one edge-triggered STATUSTEXT, plus one on
recovery. Not latched: the control loop's own armed/mode stay authoritative.

Counted in DShot cycles rather than wall time on purpose: a flash write on
Core 0 (every live param save) suspends both Core-1 tasks together, and a
millisecond age would read that shared pause as a control stall and cut the
thrusters mid-dive. The unused loop_stamp_ms (and its per-cycle mtx_control
take) is removed.

The ESP-IDF task watchdog is deliberately not subscribed: its default 5 s
timeout is irrelevant next to 20 ms and its action is a reboot at depth.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KchLnXUAMJ6S4pj3BZLobN
